<title>JAPAN: Japan Dec lead battery sales rise 6.2 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan Dec lead battery sales rise 6.2 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's sales of domestic lead batteries, measured in volume of contained lead, rose 6.2 percent in December from the same month the year before to 29,442 tonnes, the Japan Storage Battery Association said on Friday.</p>
<p>Conained lead in Japanese battery sales in December (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		     Dec 96	 yr/yr change</p>
<p> Total	     29,442	  +6.2 pct</p>
<p>   Automotive    24,320	  +5.3 pct</p>
<p>   Industrial     3,655	 +12.6 pct</p>
<p>(NOTE: Automotive includes a small quantity of lead used in two-wheeled vehicles. Industrial use includes stationary power sources and electric vehicles such as forklifts.)</p>
<p>Unit shipments of Japanese car batteries (in 1,000s):</p>
<p>		     Dec 96	 yr/yr change</p>
<p> TOTAL		2,885	  +6.1 pct</p>
<p> Domestic	   2,829	  +5.8 pct</p>
<p>   New cars	   908	  +8.1 pct</p>
<p>   Replacement    1,921	  +4.7 pct</p>
<p> Exports		 56	 +23.9 pct</p>
<p>(NOTE: Unit shipment data excludes two-wheeled vehicles.)</p>
<p>--Tokyo Commodity Desk +81-3-3432-6179</p>
</text>
